  "lineage": "The umbrella of regional Mexican string-and-voice repertoires — son jalisciense, son huasteco, son jarocho, canción ranchera — consolidated between the late colonial period and the 1930s-50s XEW radio and Peerless/Musart record era, built on 6/8-against-3/4 sesquiáltera hemiola, zapateado footwork on a wooden tarima, close two-voice falsete harmony, and a plucked-string core of vihuela, guitarrón, harp, jarana and violin, with the mariachi trumpet added only after 1930s broadcasting demanded it.",
